Risk Assessment of a Close Spaced Shield Construction
Based on Cloud Modeling
LI Wenjie1,ZHANG Zhuohao2,YU Qunzhou1,ZHOU Cheng1,XIE Danni1
(1. School of Civil and Hydraulic Engineering,National Center of Technology Innovation for Digital Construction,
Huazhong University of Science and Technology,Wuhan 430070,China,E-mail:liwenjie105@163.com;
2. School of Civil Engineering,Shandong Jianzhu University,Jinan 250101,China)
Abstract:Compared with the conventional shield construction,the construction of the rearward tunnel in close spaced shield
construction poses not only heightens difficulty and risk but also causes the structural deformation and displacement of the existing
tunnel and may jeopardize the safety of the existing tunnel. Therefore,it is necessary to identify and evaluate the risk of the close
spaced shield construction to provide support for formulating control measures. This paper draws upon the shield construction case in
the proximity of the densely spaced segment within the exceptionally large-diameter tunnel spanning the river at San yang Road of
City Railway Transit Line 7. The typical risk indicators are concluded based on the engineering features of this project,the weights
of these indicators are determined by utilizing the entropy weighting method,and each risk is assessed through the application of the
cloud model evaluation method. In actual construction,targeted measures are taken in combination with the assessment level to
ensure the safety of construction. The effectiveness and feasibility of the used method are also verified. This paper can provide
reference for the risk assessment of similar projects.
Keywords:san yang road tunnel;close spaced shield construction;existing tunnel;risk assessment;cloud modeling
随着城市轨道交通的不断建设,地铁线路网越来 越密集,并且由于既有建(构)筑物和地下管线的存 在,可利用的空间越来越少,导致双线近间距隧道越
来越多。我国《地铁设计规范》(GB50157-2013)[1] 第 11.1.12 条规定:盾构施工双线隧道的净距小于 隧道直径时,为近间距盾构施工。长期的工程经验 及相关研究表明,近间距盾构施工双线隧道之间相 互影响更大,并且后行隧道的施工会扰动周围土体
